  "caption": "India is building its semiconductor industry from the ground up.\nFour plants are going commercial by late 2026: Tata Electronics (Assam), Micron (Gujarat), CG Power, and RRP Electronics.\nCombined daily output: 80 million chips.\nTotal investment: $15.2 billion.\nDirect jobs: 28,000.\nWhat does this scale of domestic chip production mean for India's electronics supply chain?\nSources:\nReuters \u2014 https://reuters.com\n#Semiconductors #MakeInIndia #TataElectronics #Micron #IndiaManufacturing #Electronics",
